  "content": {
    "title": "Tyler Tanner, Vanderbilt basketball fall just short vs Nebraska in NCAA Tournament",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 10:49 p.m. CTVanderbilt basketball managed to take the lead for a moment in the second half, but could not hang on in the second round of the Men's NCAA Tournament.No. 4 seed Nebraska beat No. 5 seed Vanderbilt 74-72 at the Paycom Center in Oklahoma City on March 21. Braden Frager made the game-winning layup with 2.1 seconds remaining. Vanderbilt guard Tyler Tanner's miracle heave attempt rimmed out at the buzzer.Vanderbilt (27-9) missed out on returning to the Sweet 16 for the first time since 2007. Nebraska will face the winner of No. 1 Florida or No. 9 Iowa.Tanner propelled the Commodores throughout the game. The star guard finished with 27 points.The Cornhuskers (28-6) jumped out to a 14-4 lead in the opening minutes in front of a dominant Nebraska crowd. The Commodores did not take their first lead until 8:26 was left, when AK Okereke made a 3-pointer. Buy Vanderbilt basketball 2026 NCAA Tournament ticketsVanderbilt vs Nebraska score updates AK Okereke makes 3-pointer, forces Nebraska timeoutVanderbilt is up 70-68 with 1:42 remaining. AK Okereke made a corner 3-pointer. AK Okereke 3-pointer Vanderbilt first lead over NebraskaVanderbilt has its first lead of the game after AK Okereke made a 3-pointer. It put the Commodores up 58-55 with 8:26 remaining in the game. Tyler Tanner returns to game for VanderbiltVanderbilt guard Tyler Tanner was only out for a couple minutes. Tanner is back with 13 minutes remaining. Tyler Tanner injury updateVanderbilt guard Tyler Tanners was shown on the TV broadcast getting some attention on his ankle while sitting on the bench. He is out of the game for the moment. Vanderbilt pulls within four points against NebraskaThe Commodores have outscored Vanderbilt 12-9 in a hot-shooting second half for both teams. Nebraska leads 48-44 with 14:55 remaining in the game. Vanderbilt, Nebraska second half beginsVanderbilt gets the first point of the half on a free throw from Tyler Tanner. Nebraska leads 39-33. Tyler Tanner statsVanderbilt guard Tyler Tanner is keeping the Commodores in the game.He is up to 13 points, two assists and three steals. Nebraska leads 29-21 with 4:19 remaining. Tyler Tanner makes Vanderbilt's first 3-pointerTyler Tanner has 11 early points. The Commodores trail 21-15 with 8:12 remaining in the first half. Nebraska up on Vanderbilt halfway through first halfNebraska leads Vanderbilt 16-10 with 10:48 remaining in the first half.3-pointers have separated the teams. Vanderbilt is 0-for-8 from long range. Nebraska is 3-for-5. Tyler Tanner breaks Vanderbilt's single-season assist recordVanderbilt guard Tyler Tanner got his 181st assist of the season on a pass to Jalen Washington. It broke Atiba Prater's mark in 1999-00. Vanderbilt starts out ice-cold on 3-pointersNebraska leads Vanderbilt 11-4 with 15:23 remaining in the first half.Vanderbilt is 0-for-5 on 3-pointers. Tyler Tanner quiets Nebraska runNebraska got up 8-0 on Vanderbilt before star Commodores guard Tyler Tanner hit a floater to make it 8-2. Nebraska wins challenge on out of bounds callThe ball bounced out of play with 18:32 remaining in the first half. Fred Hoiberg challenged the ruling that it was off Nebraska, and he was correct. The ball was ruled off Vanderbilt's AK Okereke. Vanderbilt, Nebraska game tips offVanderbilt wins the opening tip and the game is underway. Bruce Pearls picks Vanderbilt to winStudio host Bruce Pearl, the former coach of Auburn, picked Vanderbilt to beat Nebraska in the pregame show on TNT Duke Miles injury updateVanderbilt guard Duke Miles has been listed as a starter in the pregame lineup. He has tape on his left thumb after jamming it the first round game. Expect Nebraska crowd to provide a healthy advantageThe Nebraska fans have traveled well to Oklahoma City. Those cheering for the Cornhuskers are being vocal in warmups. Vanderbilt vs Nebraska start timeThe Commodores and Cornhuskers will tip off at 7:58 p.m., according to the countdown clock in the arena. Vanderbilt vs Nebraska starting lineupsNebraskaGuard Sam HoibergGuard Jamarques LawrenceForward Berke BuyuktuncelForward Pryce SandfortForward Rienk MastVanderbiltGuard Duke MilesGuard Tyler TannerForward Tyler NickelForward AK OkerekeForward Devin McGlocktonWhen does Vanderbilt basketball vs Nebraska start?Date: Saturday, March 21Time: 7:45 p.m. CTWhere: Paycom Center, Oklahoma CityWhat channel is Vanderbilt basketball vs Nebraska on today?TV Channel: TruTVLive stream: SlingVanderbilt basketball schedule (last five games)March 7: W 86-82 at TennesseeMarch 13: W 75-68 vs. Tennessee in SEC TournamentMarch 14: W 91-74 vs. Florida in SEC TournamentMarch 15: L 86-75 vs. Arkansas in SEC TournamentMarch 19: W 78-68 vs. McNeese State in NCAA TournamentSam Hutchens covers sports for the Clarion Ledger. Email him at Shutchens@gannett.com or reach him on X at @Sam_Hutchens_",
